    "name": "Sedum Palmeri Succulents",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Sedum palmeri is a species in the family Crassulaceae native to Mexico with persistent light green leaves, becoming marked with red during winter. The plant is about 30cm high and 40 cm wide, and forms a rounded cushion with leaves arranged in rosettes located at the tips of stems. These plants come in a plastic baggie in a berry pint, you can remove the plastic and put the plant plus the recycled berry pint into the ground to decompose and grow!</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Contains 5 starter stalks.</span></p>",
